Third-party campus-digital-twin dashboards (GIS, sensor panels, control-room style) look similar because they reuse the same sparse primitive set: a bird's-eye or isometric building footprint overlay, fixed/floating labels, live KPI panels, table-style event rows, and one persistent control strip. The attached reference is one instance of that family — the structure, not the proprietary detail.

This document maps the pattern to the existing MIRRORWORLD frontend, then gives a concrete, incremental architecture to reach the same visual tier without changing the backend or the rest of the application.

## 1. What the reference is actually showing

Section by section, the attached screen is:

- **Header strip:** title, weather/health widget, user pill, clock/date. Pure chrome with no backend dependency.
- **Central spatial view:** stylized top-down/isometric campus with buildings, roads, water, courts, trees, floating building tags carrying area and live status, a map-control toggle, a "tour/immersion" button, and an emergency badge. This is the core.
- **Left panel stack:** asset information (with sub-tabs and values), department ranking bar chart, equipment-fault table.
- **Right panel stack:** energy/water  [… 5,566 characters omitted] hing management, asset operations). That strip should navigate or toggle views, not be a second router.

## 6. Data contract

Rely on or extend these existing contracts:

- `/api/campus` — buildings, rooms, schedule, summary, baseline.
- `/api/overview` — metrics and alert counts.
- `/api/alerts` — alert list with severity, category, title, detail, affected resources.
- `/api/movement` — transition estimates if you want live flow overlay.

If a new panel needs a value that does not exist yet (for example building area, parking counts, per-building energy), add the smallest possible backend field or endpoint and seed it from campus data or a clearly labeled assumption. Do not invent numbers in the UI.

## 7. Implementation order

1. Build the expanded SVG map first: more blocks, area tags, status chips, map fixtures, map toggle, tour button, emergency badge. Reuse `DigitalCampusPage` selection/flows.
